        ":question/problem": "Given that $f(x)={(3x+4)}^{5},$ find ${f}^{\u2032}(x).$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let $g(x)=3x+4$ and $f(g(x))=g(x{)}^{5}.$ \n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(g(x)) & =({g}^{5}{)}^{\u2032}=5{g}^{4}, \\\\ {g}^{\u2032}(x) & =(3x+4{)}^{\u2032}=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the chain rule, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\u2032}(x) & ={f}^{\u2032}(g(x))\\cdot {g}^{\u2032}(x) \\\\  & =5{g}^{4}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =15(3x+4{)}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
